","edition":"2026-08","publisher":"Office for National Statistics","licence":{"name":"Open Government Licence v3.0","url":"https://example.com/ogl"},"attribution":["Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right"]},"note":"A postcode is placed by the single centroid the ONS Postcode Directory gives it. Its addresses can fall on both sides of a boundary, so an area containing the centroid need not contain every address in the postcode. Containment is tested against each release's published geometry, not against surveyed ground. A point on an edge belongs to every area sharing it and is labelled boundary. nearBoundary marks a match whose edge lies within positionalToleranceM, the sum of the coordinate's written precision, the boundary's generalisation and the accuracy of any transformation to WGS 84; there, a more precise coordinate or boundary could change the answer. Release-wide geometry provenance is given once in releases; a match lists corrections only where one moved that area."},"meta":{"nextCursor":null}}
